WEBVTT

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.410
Tada Coffee Shop

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.620
Well, see you later, Nyanko Big.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.660
Meow!

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:33.750
Sakuradamon Gate

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.250
Say cheese!

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.540
Cheese!

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.830
Wow, it's so beautiful!

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:20.620
Excuse me!

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:21.410
Huh?!

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:23.950
Could you take my picture?

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.330
Huh? Uh...

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.830
I can't speak English.

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:33.540
Huh?

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.410
Oh, was my Japanese wrong?

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:41.160
Huh? Uh, no, yes, okay.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.000
Thank you!

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:45.580
Insufficient Battery Power

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.580
I can't take it.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.250
Huh?

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.660
Um, what do you mean?

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.580
The battery's dead.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:57.660
Huh? But the battery icon was blinking like crazy earlier.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:58.870
Right.

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:00.950
Do you have a spare battery?

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:06.700
I got separated from my companion, so I unfortunately

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:06.700
don't have my luggage or any of my belongings.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.540
What?

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:12.330
Sorry, you can't take my picture with that, huh?

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.120
Sorry for bothering you.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.580
Then, your memory card...

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:23.330
Huh?

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:27.620
Why don't I take a picture with my camera

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:27.620
and your memory card, then give it to you?

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.660
Are you sure?!

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:33.870
Okay, I'm gonna take your picture!

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:36.290
Okay! Please go ahead!

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:39.160
This foreigner is weird...

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:43.500
I sincerely appreciate it.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.450
I'll never forget your kindness!

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.910
"Sincerely appreciate it"?

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:52.790
Huh?

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:56.870
Wait, what am I gonna do with her memory card?!

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:08.700
Tada Never Falls in Love

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:32.040
I Can't Just Leave You

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.660
Looks like it's gonna rain.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:40.790
Wait!

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:42.540
Excuse me!

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.000
We meet again!

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:49.120
Uh, yeah...

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:50.250
Here you go.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:55.200
I really, sincerely appreciate it!

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:55.200
I will be sure to repay your kindness!

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.790
You don't have to.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:58.950
I'll give this back, though.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:03.870
I totally forgot about this. Thank you very much.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.790
Well, take care.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:07.790
Hey, that's...

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:08.500
Huh?

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.040
...the Shogun's secret passage!

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.620
It's marvelous! It's the genuine article!

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.200
Hold on!

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:17.290
Huh?

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:21.790
That's a sluice gate, but it's not really

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:21.790
a secret passage or anything like that.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:27.540
Huh? But Rainbow Shogun sneaks out

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:27.540
of the castle by using that passage!

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.700
Rainbow Shogun...?

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:32.370
Of course, you know about that, right?

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:39.790
Rainbow Shogun.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:44.290
Rainbow Shogun

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:49.290
Rainbow Shogun is a historical

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:49.290
action drama on social reform,

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:49.290
Starring

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:54.080
in which Edo bakufu Tokugawa Nijimune

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:54.080
slays the evil that overruns Edo.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.080
Tokugawa Nijimune

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.080
Ryoji Takeshita

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.830
State one color of the rainbow!

00:05:58.500 --> 00:05:59.950
R-red...

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:03.580
The color of the rainbow is rainbow! Meet your maker!

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:11.250
Always make your heart rainbow!

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:12.870
To be continued

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.250
"Rainbow!"

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.500
He says that at the end!

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.000
Right...

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:20.450
That explains the things you've been doing...

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:22.500
I do know what Rainbow Shogun is, though.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.700
It's really popular in Japan, right?

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:26.750
Maybe...?

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:27.790
Well, then!

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:28.870
Hold on!

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:33.040
That's a work of fiction!

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:33.040
If you go in there, you'll be arrested!

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.500
So, I can't go?

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.200
You understood me...

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:42.330
But since I was able to come all the way

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:42.330
to the place I'd dreamed of...

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:43.870
I'll inscribe it in my memory!

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.250
Well, anyway... take care.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.410
Come here. You'll catch a cold.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.580
You're safe now.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:23.750
Meow.

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:29.200
Y-you're safe.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.080
Y-you're safe.

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:43.410
Where are you headed?

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:44.410
Huh?

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:45.910
I'll walk you home.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.700
Ginza, I think.

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:51.750
You think?

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:55.160
I left everything with my companion, so...

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:59.080
I can't get there based on that, huh?

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.660
I-I'm fine!

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:07.370
You're not fine, no matter how you look at this.

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:11.290
Let's go to my grandpa's shop. It's nearby, anyway.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:12.410
But...

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:15.160
I can't just leave you like this.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:27.790
I cannot leave you like this.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:32.040
It's polite to quietly accept a favor.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.370
Could you be Rainbow Shogun?

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:38.330
No.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:40.410
Thank you very much!

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:43.870
Always make your heart rainbow!

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:45.450
To be continued.

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:49.330
Brought to you by these sponsors.

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:50.790
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:54.700
I'm back.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.080
You're late, Big Bro! You're tardy!

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:02.540
Tada Coffee Shop

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.290
Welcome back.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:02.540
You said you'd call me if you're gonna be late!

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:05.410
Sorry, it started raining all of a sudden.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.410
Meow.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:08.830
Geez! What do you even have a smartphone for?

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.160
Sorry, come on in.

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:20.700
Who's that?! What, your girlfriend?!

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:21.660
No.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:26.290
Grandpa, she seems hungry,

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:26.290
so could you serve her something to eat?

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:28.330
S-sure. What's your name?

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:31.330
Nice to meet you. I'm Teresa Du...

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:35.200
Teresa Wagner.

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:41.700
Wow! She's beautiful!

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:46.330
Welcome to the Tada Coffee Shop! I'm Yui Tada!

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:50.410
And this is Grandpa, Nyanko Big, and Big Bro!

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:52.790
Wait, you already know that, huh?

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:59.450
Yes. Yui-san, Grandpa-san,

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:59.450
Nyanko Big-san, and Big Bro-san.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:01.540
It's Mitsuyoshi Tada.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.790
Mitsuyoshi Tada-san.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:11.700
You're gonna catch a cold like that.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:11.700
Yui, give her something to change into.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:12.750
Okay!

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:18.120
I sincerely appreciate it, everyone.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:18.120
I will never forget your kindness!

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:27.370
I knew it. There's no way Big Bro can score a girlfriend.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:31.120
Oh, I'll throw your clothes into the washer.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:33.200
Thank you very much.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.040
Sure!

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:38.200
And may I borrow your phone?

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.330
Sure, it's on the table there!

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:53.870
Hello? Thank goodness the call went through!

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.870
Roster

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.870
Meals          Laundry

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.870
Nyanko's, too!                Hang Dry

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.870
Grandpa   Big Brother

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.870
Yui

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:56.870
Thank you very much.

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:03.290
It's very delicious!

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:11.160
It's unusual for shy ol' Nyanko Big to approach strangers.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:12.330
Really?

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:13.290
Meow!

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:16.790
Nyanko Big does love pretty girls, after all.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:18.500
Meow!

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:29.290
Heya, Mitsuyoshi! Please give me the usual!

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:31.870
Welcome, Kaoru-kun.

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:34.540
Can't you come in more like a normal person?

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:38.830
Well, my charm just overflows no matter what.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:42.250
One special coffee jelly and one blended coffee!

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:43.120
Coming right up!

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:44.450
Hey, Nyanko Big!

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:45.700
Hiss!

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:47.080
Whoa!

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.620
Th-that was close!

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:56.500
That is today's update for Trepid Nyanko Big's blog, huh?

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:59.000
Trepid Nyanko Big?

00:11:59.000 --> 00:11:59.870
This!

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:01.830
Today's Trepid Nyanko Big

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:01.830
Today's Trepid Nyanko Big

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.120
Today's Trepid Nyanko Big

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:04.250
Today's Trepid Nyanko Big

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:07.790
My! So, he's a fighting samurai cat, huh?

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:08.580
Meow.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:14.250
Oh? Who's the blonde mademoiselle?

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:18.200
Or should I say, I'm glad to meet you.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:20.540
Who are you trying to impress?

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:22.790
She's a customer. Big Bro's customer.

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:29.200
Mitsuyoshi's?! His girlfriend?! For real?!

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:29.200
You're lying! You never told me!

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:30.540
She's not my girlfriend.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:37.120
Is your blonde hair real?

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:39.330
Hey, Ijuin...

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:41.540
Teresa?!

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:45.040
Step away from her!

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.200
Alec?!

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:11.330
I am Alexandra Magritte.

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:16.660
I am truly sorry. I was certain Teresa was being attacked.

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:20.120
Alec, this is when you kowtow!

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:23.120
Kowtow? Understood.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:24.370
Eek!

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:26.790
Oh, everything's okay now, so...

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:32.700
Everything's not okay! What's up with her,

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:32.700
Mitsuyoshi?! She's super scary!

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.410
It's your fault.

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:36.290
Excuse me?! How?!

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:39.040
I'm really sorry, Ijuin-san.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:44.370
Oh, it's all good! It's no big deal since

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:44.370
you're worried about me, Teresa-chan.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:52.540
It hurts so much! I'm gonna cry!

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:54.450
I'm already crying!

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:58.830
Really? So, you got separated by

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:58.830
changing trains at the Tokyo Station.

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:02.040
Even after I told you not to go off on your own...

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:03.870
I'm sorry.

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:08.290
I noticed you weren't with me after riding the subway.

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:11.370
But I didn't have any money,

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:11.370
even though I wanted to go back.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.830
But I saw a castle, so...

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:17.450
I just...

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:22.500
"To err is human."

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:31.870
"However, the mistakes made become one of

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:31.870
the enrichments in this journey called life."

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:33.250
Wow!

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:34.160
Pardon me?

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:35.750
Those are lovely words!

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:36.620
Right?!

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:39.750
Illustration: Rachel Lo

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:39.750
Sunflower

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:39.750
Express

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:39.750
-A Police Blotter in Love-

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:39.750
A Beautiful Master

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:39.750
Detective Appears

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:39.700
Those were Yoshiko Yamamura Poiron's words from

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:42.500
Sunflower Express: A Police Blotter in Love.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:44.500
A police blotter in love?

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:47.040
Do you read it?! I'll lend this to you!

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:48.870
Thank you.

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:53.250
Anyway, you both are really good at speaking Japanese.

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:55.910
I watched and learned the language

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:55.910
from Rainbow Shogun.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:15:00.540
What?! Grandpa loves Rainbow Shogun, too, right?!

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:04.620
My! It's popular here, too, huh?!

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:07.160
They have reruns in the evening.

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:10.160
Tada Coffee Shop

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:11.290
Mitsuyoshi, does Rainbow Shogun air overseas?

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:12.660
I don't know.

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:16.200
Anyway, Teresa-chan, what country are you from?

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:18.580
Larsenburg.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:22.250
What?! That's the country

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:22.250
Yoshiko Yamamura Poiron is from!

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:25.080
Wait, where is Larsenburg located?

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:31.580
It's a small country in Europe. It's a beautiful

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:31.580
country full of valleys and greenery. Right?

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:32.870
Yes!

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:38.500
Huh... sounds pretty nice.

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:38.500
It'd be nice to visit. Right, Mitsuyoshi?

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:40.000
Huh? Yeah...

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:43.580
Oh, yeah, you're afraid of heights.

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:46.500
That's why Big Bro is also afraid of riding airplanes.

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:49.750
It's not that I'm scared. I just don't want to ride on them.

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:50.910
Same difference!

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:55.500
That's funny, isn't it, Teresa-chan?

00:15:57.870 --> 00:15:59.500
It's time for us to take our leave.

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:02.950
I will visit again and offer my thanks someday.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:06.870
Everyone, I sincerely appreciate it.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:06.870
I will repay you for all the things you've done for me.

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:08.500
Goodbye.

00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:09.830
See you later!

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:13.370
Pretty foreign girls sure are nice!

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:15.120
Huh?

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:16.000
What is it?

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:19.750
Ijuin, you've got a black eye.

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:20.500
Huh?!

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:24.450
What the hell?!

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:30.250
The girls will cry if they see what happened

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:30.250
to Ginza's number one Adonis' face!

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:34.000
That's not true. You look like a one-eyed panda. It's cute.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:36.910
Huh? For real?! It's not that bad? The black eye is okay?

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:38.450
Yeah, you'll be fine!

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:39.410
Uh-huh!

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:39.790
It's okay?

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:44.160
Nekoya

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:47.120
Why are there so many people here?

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:50.040
There are more people here than

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:50.040
on a festival day in Larsenburg.

00:16:52.410 --> 00:16:56.080
The Shogun's castle was like this, too. And it rained.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:17:00.290
If Tada-san hadn't helped me out,

00:16:56.450 --> 00:17:00.290
I might not have been able to meet up with you.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.580
What were you going to do if we hadn't met up?!

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:07.330
Chuo

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:11.200
Miss Teresa.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:12.200
Yes?

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:15.620
Please get your act together. Someday, you'll be...

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:22.660
Please be more responsible.

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:25.250
Yes. I'll be careful.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:31.830
Are you listening?

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:33.200
Yes!

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:43.120
That's strange. It should be around here.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:46.370
Chuo

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:46.000
Didn't we go down this street just a little while ago?

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:50.040
Is that the map Rachel drew up?

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.040
Yes.

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:54.450
This is difficult, huh?

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:56.500
Yes...

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:03.660
Mitsuyoshi! What concentration did you go with

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:03.660
for the next photography contest?

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:05.750
I haven't decided yet.

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:07.870
My concentration will obviously be me.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:12.870
Aren't you getting tired of taking pictures of just yourself?

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:13.750
Nope, not at all!

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:19.370
I'm so deep of a concentration that

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:19.370
it's impossible to represent me that easily.

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:22.580
Well, you have a black eye today,

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:22.580
so it might be interesting.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:26.540
Hey, this looks like Teresa-chan, doesn't it?

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:31.910
Speak of the devil.

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:40.790
Huh? Oh! Whoa! I can't believe we meet again!

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:40.790
We must be soulmates!

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:43.950
Just kidding!

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:46.250
I want to go here.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:48.950
Is this a map?

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:54.620
It says, "Grand Palace Ginza,"

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:54.620
so I think it's probably a mansion.

00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:56.040
A mansion?

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:57.250
Yes.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:59.950
Is that where you two are staying?

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:01.160
Yes.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:01.950
Seriously?!

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.450
Do you know of it?

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.290
I do. It's...

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:07.790
Tada Coffee Shop

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.250
...this place.

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:11.950
This place?!

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:15.580
H-he's not lying! It says right here!

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:20.200
The Grand Palace Ginza

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:20.200
Alec pictured

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:19.660
No way. This can't be! This is the Grand Palace?

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:28.120
Alec, I like the Grand Palace Ginza.

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.660
But Teresa...

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:34.790
Besides, there's a delicious coffee shop

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:34.790
next door, so it's fine.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:37.790
Yeah, that's right!

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:40.910
Come by anytime for a drink at Tada Coffee Shop!

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:42.790
I'm almost always there, after all!

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.790
I mean, I'm there once in a while!

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:55.000
Thank you very much. I really, sincerely appreciate

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:55.000
everything you've done for me today.

00:19:56.200 --> 00:19:59.620
Let's be good neighbors from here on out!

00:19:59.620 --> 00:20:01.870
Hey, you're not their neighbor.

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:05.370
Thank you!

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:23.620
Oh, this photo...

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.370
Meow.

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:31.040
Is this a good photo?

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:34.120
I feel like I've seen those eyes before somewhere.

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:38.450
Her eyes are green like yours, Nyanko Big.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:40.370
Meow!

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:45.950
Miss Teresa?

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:48.540
It's the North Star, Alec.

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:49.200
Huh?

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:53.750
Tokyo is so bright, but we can still see

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:53.750
the stars in the sky, huh?

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:58.870
It’s a lucky sign that always shows us the way.

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:04.660
That's true. Although, we started things off

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:04.660
with a bunch of unexpected events.

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:08.450
It's "always make your heart rainbow!"

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:13.040
I've dreamed of visiting Japan,

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:13.040
and I'm sure there are a lot of exciting things to come!

00:22:44.620 --> 00:22:46.000
Mitsuyoshi!

00:22:47.750 --> 00:22:49.290
Your black eye healed.

00:22:49.750 --> 00:22:52.410
Resilience is the most important thing for an Adonis.

00:22:53.830 --> 00:22:58.120
Everyone, I'll introduce you to

00:22:53.830 --> 00:22:58.120
our transfer students from overseas today.

00:22:59.290 --> 00:23:00.500
Overseas?!

00:23:00.750 --> 00:23:01.620
Overseas...?

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:03.660
Huh? Overseas?

00:23:09.870 --> 00:23:14.040
Teresa Wagner-san and Alexandra Magritte-san.

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:17.910
T..Teresa-chan and... Alec-san?!

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:19.870
Eep!

00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:23.870
Nice to meet you!

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:29.410
Mitsuyoshi, the transfer students from overseas

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:29.410
was a shocker, wasn't it?

00:23:29.410 --> 00:23:30.000
Yeah.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:31.660
I want to be a transfer student who's the talk of the town.

00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:33.080
You're not okay with just being

00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:33.080
an ordinary transfer student?

00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:36.660
Being an ordinary one is boring!

00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:36.660
Well, you're always ordinary, Mitsuyoshi.

00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:39.620
Next time: Episode 2, "Well, It's Not Wrong."

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:41.000
Well, It's Not Wrong

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:41.000
Please look forward to it.
